Files expected in /home/ubuntu/fwm-backup/secrets/ on the backup server (root, mode 700; never in git):

restic-password      32+ random characters, e.g. `openssl rand -base64 32`. Also store it in your password manager.
id_ed25519           Private SSH key for production: `ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -N '' -C fwm-backup -f id_ed25519`
known_hosts          Production's host key, pinned: `ssh-keyscan -t ed25519 <prod-address> > known_hosts`
ssh_config           See below
telegram-bot-token   The bot token (same bot as Grafana)
telegram-chat-id     The chat ID

ssh_config:

Host prod
    HostName <prod-address>
    User fwm-backup
    IdentityFile /secrets/id_ed25519
    UserKnownHostsFile /secrets/known_hosts
    StrictHostKeyChecking yes
    Compression yes
    ServerAliveInterval 30
    # Production's OpenSSH (< 9.0) has no post-quantum key exchange; silences the client warning for this host only
    WarnWeakCrypto no-pq-kex
